<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net9.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>

    <PackageId>TheKrystalShip.KGSM.Lib</PackageId>
    <Authors>Heisenberg</Authors>
    <Version>1.8.0</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>1.8.0 — Event origin + caller-supplied lifecycle provenance. Completes the audit-provenance pair started in 1.6.0: the event envelope (EventWrapper) and EventDataBase now also surface Origin (string?) — the surface that drove the event (ui|assistant|discord|system|api), the companion to Actor (who) answering "through which surface". EventService copies it from the envelope onto each dispatched event-data object, like Actor/Timestamp. KGSM takes it from $KGSM_EVENT_ORIGIN; unlike the actor there is NO fallback for a bare CLI call (no product surface), so an absent origin stays null — never fabricated. To let a caller actually stamp this, ILifecycleService.Start/Stop/Restart gain optional (actor, origin) parameters that are propagated to KGSM as $KGSM_EVENT_ACTOR/$KGSM_EVENT_ORIGIN for that one invocation (new IProcessRunner/IKgsmCommandExecutor environment overloads layer them onto the child process, never mutating the lib's own environment); omitted values fall back to KGSM's own honest defaults. Additive and non-breaking: the new params default to null, a pre-origin payload deserializes Origin as null, and existing call sites compile unchanged. AOT-safe (Origin is a property of the already-registered EventWrapper; provenance is plain env vars). — 1.7.0 — Unified ecosystem health probe. WatchdogClient now probes the watchdog's GET /health (was /ready) for both IsReadyAsync and GetReadyAsync; the daemon serves /health as the canonical readiness path (200 ready / 503 + reason) and keeps /ready as a deprecated alias for one transition release, so a consumer still on 1.6.0 keeps working unchanged. Response shape is unchanged ({ready,detail} → WatchdogReadyState) and no method signature changed — additive and non-breaking. Part of standardizing every ecosystem leaf on a single GET /health. — 1.6.0 — Event audit enrichment (who/when). The event envelope (EventWrapper) now surfaces the top-level metadata KGSM already emits but the lib previously dropped: Timestamp (DateTimeOffset?), Actor (string?), Hostname (string?), and KgsmVersion (string?, bound from the wire's KGSMVersion). EventDataBase gains Timestamp + Actor, and EventService copies them from the envelope onto each dispatched event-data object — so handlers see who triggered an event and when, with no handler-signature change. Actor is the audit principal: KGSM takes it from $KGSM_EVENT_ACTOR (set by the calling surface — bot/assistant/watchdog) or falls back to the invoking OS user; null/absent is preserved as null, never a fabricated identity or time. Additive and non-breaking: a pre-enrichment payload leaves the new fields null. This is the consumer half of the event-enrichment work (kgsm emits, lib surfaces); event *persistence* lives downstream of the stateless engine. — 1.5.0 — Native cgroup path, plus the first package to ship three already-committed post-1.4.0 changes. NEW: Instance.CgroupPath — the per-instance cgroup v2 directory KGSM derives for a native instance (kgsm.slice/&lt;name&gt;), the exact path kgsm-watchdog (re)creates on every native start; empty for container instances (Docker owns their cgroup) and when KGSM omits the field. Lets kgsm-monitor read native cgroup counters directly (CPU/mem/pids/io) instead of the /proc process-tree fallback, without re-deriving the cgroup layout or opening the watchdog socket — additive, JSON without cgroup_path deserializes CgroupPath as empty. ALSO FIRST PACKAGED HERE (committed on main after the 1.4.0 cut): (1) Reading&lt;T&gt; typed-unknown envelope — **BREAKING**: GetAllStatuses now returns Dictionary&lt;string, Reading&lt;InstanceRuntimeStatus&gt;&gt; (was Dictionary&lt;string, InstanceRuntimeStatus&gt;); (2) InstanceService.GetInstanceConfigValue/SetInstanceConfigValue — read/write a single key in an instance .config.ini; (3) typed host SystemInfo model + ISystemService.GetSystemInfo(). — 1.4.0 — Blueprint game metadata. Blueprint gains a nullable Metadata object (BlueprintMetadata: DisplayName, Description, MaxPlayers, MinRamMb, RecommendedRamMb, BaseDiskMb) mirroring the new nested "Metadata" block emitted by `kgsm blueprints info --json`. All values are nullable: an unknown value is null, never a fabricated 0. Additive and non-breaking — JSON from older KGSM without the block deserializes Metadata as null. (KGSM itself moved to a unified per-game .bp.yaml blueprint format, but the lib only ever consumes the JSON wire shape, which is unchanged except for the added Metadata object.) — 1.3.0 — BREAKING: systemd removed as a KGSM instance lifecycle manager. Deleted the LifecycleManager enum and Instance.LifecycleManager/EnableSystemd/SystemdServiceFile/SystemdSocketFile/SystemdUnit, ConfigurationInfo.LifecycleManager, and the LifecycleManager field on the instance-started/stopped/restarted event payloads. Instance.Runtime (native|container) is now the sole supervision discriminator. Legacy lifecycle_manager/systemd_* JSON fields older KGSM still emits are tolerated (unmapped, ignored). — 1.2.0: Typed kgsm-watchdog control client (IWatchdogClient / WatchdogClient): start/stop/status/list/ready over the daemon's unix socket (HTTP/1.1 via SocketsHttpHandler.ConnectCallback), reflection-free source-generated JSON (Native AOT/trim-safe), registered via AddKgsmWatchdogClient. — 1.1.0: Bulk fleet status read (GetAllStatuses, with --fast); restart and *-failed event types; reflection-free source-generated JSON for Native AOT/trim safety.</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/TheKrystalShip/KGSM-Lib</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/TheKrystalShip/KGSM-Lib</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>GitHub</RepositoryType>
    <Description>Classlibrary for KGSM Interop</Description>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>GPL-3.0-only</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <NeutralLanguage>en</NeutralLanguage>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <RootNamespace>TheKrystalShip.KGSM</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>TheKrystalShip.KGSM</AssemblyName>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <DocumentationFile>bin\$(Configuration)\$(TargetFramework)\$(AssemblyName).xml</DocumentationFile>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
      <None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\"/>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection" Version="9.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Extensions.Logging.Abstractions" Version="9.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
